<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gil González Dávila</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1480–<a href="/years/1526">1526</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gil González Dávila was a Spanish conquistador who led the first Spanish expedition into what is now Costa Rica and Nicaragua in 1522–1523. He met the chiefs of Nicoya and Nicarao, who accepted baptism, and gathered much gold. Later conflicts with rival Spanish captains over control of Nicaragua and Honduras ended with his return to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gil-gonzalez-davila.jpg" alt="Gil González Dávila" width="252" height="318" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author, subject died in 1526 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gil_Gonzalez_Davila.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
